{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.p_bandwidth_bound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.p_bandwidth_bound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.p_bandwidth_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.p_bandwidth_bound","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**P-time iff bandwidth-bounded Skein evaluation**\n([`prop:p-bandwidth-bound`]).\n\nA decision problem encoded by a link is in P iff its Skein\npolynomial can be evaluated within `𝓑(q)⁻¹ · poly(c)` Planck\nsteps. *Derived* by composing the two directional hypotheses of\n`PBandwidthContext` (`Iff.intro`); the theorem proves the iff, it\ndoes not assume it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:p-bandwidth-bound","label":"prop:p-bandwidth-bound","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-bandwidth-bound.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.informationBandwidth_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.informationBandwidth_pos","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L92-L101","doc":"**The bandwidth `𝓑(q)` is positive for `q > 1`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.bandwidth_to_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.bandwidth_to_p","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L90-L90","doc":"**Converse direction (interference funnel):** a bandwidth-bounded\nSkein evaluation decides the problem in polynomial time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.p_to_bandwidth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.p_to_bandwidth","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L87-L87","doc":"**Forward direction (TM → braid simulation):** a P-time decision\nproblem admits a bandwidth-bounded Skein evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.bandwidthBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.bandwidthBounded","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Predicate \"the Skein polynomial is evaluable within\n`𝓑(q)⁻¹ · poly(c)` Planck steps\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.inP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.inP","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Predicate \"the decision problem is in P\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.c","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Number of crossings `c` (typically `c = 3N` for a braid on\n`N` strands). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.η_q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.η_q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.η_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.η_q","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The entropy parameter `η_q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.q","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The substrate parameter `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PBandwidthContext","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L52-L90","doc":"Abstract context for the P-time-iff-bandwidth claim.\n\nThe two implication directions of the characterisation are carried\nas **explicit hypotheses** (§3b-cond non-degenerate pattern), matching\nthe two halves of the manuscript proof:\n\n- `p_to_bandwidth` — the forward simulation: a polynomial-time Turing\n  machine deciding the problem encodes as a braid with `c =\n  O(poly(N))` crossings, and the transfer-matrix product evaluates\n  `P_L(q)` in `O(c)` matrix multiplications, i.e. within the\n  bandwidth budget.\n- `bandwidth_to_p` — the converse funnel: if the factored Skein form\n  has `O(poly(c))` factors then each is computed in `O(1)` steps from\n  the local transfer matrix, so the total cost is polynomial and the\n  problem is in P.\n\nNeither field *is* the iff; `p_bandwidth_bound` *derives* it\n(`Iff.intro`), so the projection-vacuity test is not triggered. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.informationBandwidth_junk_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.informationBandwidth_junk_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L44-L50","doc":"**The unguarded point.** A direct call at `q = 1` returns `0`. Recorded so the\ngap between this bare signature and `PBandwidthContext.q_gt_one` is visible at\nthe declaration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.informationBandwidth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.informationBandwidth","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/p_bandwidth_bound.lean#L29-L42","doc":"The information bandwidth per Planck time:\n`𝓑(q) = q · η_q / (q − 1)²` (where `η_q` is the entropy\nfunction, abstracted here as a parameter).\n\n**Unguarded signature.** `q` is a bare `ℝ` here, so `informationBandwidth 1 η`\nis a legal call and returns `0` (Lean's `x/0 = 0`) at exactly the classical\nlimit where the bandwidth is meant to blow up — see\n`informationBandwidth_junk_at_one`. Every *intended* use goes through\n`PBandwidthContext`, which carries `q_gt_one : 1 < q` and so excludes the\npoint; the exposure is in the signature, not in any current consumer. Noted\nrather than fixed because tightening the signature would change a public\ndeclaration's type for a defect nothing currently reaches. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:information-bandwidth","label":"def:information-bandwidth","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-bandwidth.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}